{"reviewer_participant_id":"actor:dependence-free-batch-h2-reviewer-fable-38","reviews":[{"case_id":"case:892d8dfacbc80c013262","verdict":"no_demonstrated_issue_within_scope","bounded_statement":null,"root_cause":null,"issue_class":null,"evidence_atoms":[{"description":"The workflow groups the 48 session rows by the declared independent-unit column digester_id, accumulating each vessel's four session yields into one list keyed by the unit, so repeated rows are never treated as separate analysis units.","observed_value":"sessions dict keyed by digester_id; four yields appended per vessel","source_spans":[{"path":"workflow/analysis.py","start_line":30,"end_line":33,"quoted_text":"unit = record[UNIT_COL].strip()\n            if unit not in sessions:\n                sessions[unit] = (record[ARM_COL].strip(), [])\n            sessions[unit][1].append(float(record[YIELD_COL]))"},{"path":"workflow/analysis.py","start_line":20,"end_line":20,"quoted_text":"UNIT_COL = \"digester_id\""}]},{"description":"Each digester is collapsed to a single across-session mean before any inferential procedure, yielding exactly one analysed value per independent vessel.","observed_value":"12 vessel-level means (one per digester)","source_spans":[{"path":"workflow/analysis.py","start_line":37,"end_line":43,"quoted_text":"def digester_table(sessions):\n    \"\"\"One analysed row per independent vessel: its across-session mean yield.\"\"\"\n    table = []\n    for unit in sorted(sessions):\n        arm, yields = sessions[unit]\n        table.append((unit, arm, len(yields), float(np.mean(yields))))\n    return table"}]},{"description":"The Mann-Whitney U test is applied to the arm-wise arrays drawn from the vessel-level table (6 thermal means vs 6 control means), not to the 48 raw session rows.","observed_value":"mannwhitneyu(thermal, control) on 6-vs-6 vessel means","source_spans":[{"path":"workflow/analysis.py","start_line":109,"end_line":113,"quoted_text":"control = arm_values(table, \"control\")\n    thermal = arm_values(table, \"thermal\")\n\n    u_stat, p_value = stats.mannwhitneyu(\n        thermal, control, alternative=\"two-sided\", method=\"exact\")"},{"path":"workflow/analysis.py","start_line":46,"end_line":47,"quoted_text":"def arm_values(table, arm):\n    return np.array([row[3] for row in table if row[1] == arm], dtype=float)"}]},{"description":"The reported test statistics are numerically consistent only with a 6-vs-6 vessel-level test: U = 36.0 is the maximum attainable with n1 = n2 = 6 (6*6 = 36), and the exact two-sided p = 0.002165 equals 2/C(12,6) = 2/924, the value for complete separation of the two sets of six vessel means. A row-level test on 48 records could not produce these values (max U would be 24*24 = 576).","observed_value":"U = 36.0; exact two-sided p = 0.002165 = 2/924","source_spans":[{"path":"results/report.md","start_line":42,"end_line":43,"quoted_text":"Mann-Whitney U (thermal vs control): 36.0\nExact two-sided p-value: 0.002165"},{"path":"results/report.md","start_line":45,"end_line":45,"quoted_text":"[selected-result] Thermally pretreated digesters produced higher specific methane yield than control digesters (Mann-Whitney U = 36.0, n = 6 vs 6 digester means, exact two-sided p = 0.002165); the median digester mean was 42.55 mL CH4 / g VS higher in the thermal arm."}]},{"description":"The report's per-vessel means reproduce exactly from the raw CSV rows (e.g., DG01: (268.3+251.1+271.4+258.4)/4 = 262.3; DG09: (244.6+228.5+250.6+234.3)/4 = 239.5), confirming the analysed values are one aggregated number per digester.","observed_value":"recomputed DG01 = 262.3, DG09 = 239.5; all 12 table means match","source_spans":[{"path":"results/report.md","start_line":22,"end_line":22,"quoted_text":"| DG01 | control | 4 | 262.3 |"},{"path":"data/input.csv","start_line":2,"end_line":5,"quoted_text":"DG01,control,6,268.3,7.42,812\nDG01,control,10,251.1,7.38,894\nDG01,control,14,271.4,7.45,760\nDG01,control,18,258.4,7.51,705"}]},{"description":"The workflow's aggregation matches the intended use stated in the data description: average each vessel's four session yields and compare the twelve vessel-level values between arms.","observed_value":"workflow follows the prescribed digester-level comparison","source_spans":[{"path":"data-description.md","start_line":18,"end_line":18,"quoted_text":"Independent unit column: digester_id"},{"path":"data-description.md","start_line":27,"end_line":30,"quoted_text":"Any comparison between the control and thermal arms should be made at the level\nof the digester. The usual route is to average each vessel's four session yields\ninto a single vessel-level value and then compare the twelve vessel-level values\nbetween arms, so that each independent reactor contributes exactly one number to"}]}],"counterevidence_atoms":[{"description":"The input file is long-format with the same independent unit repeated four times (48 rows for 12 digesters), and the description states these repeated rows are not independent, so the raw table would enable the issue class if fed directly into a row-independent test; however, the workflow aggregates before testing, so this remains only a latent risk, not a demonstrated issue.","observed_value":"4 rows per digester_id in data/input.csv (e.g., DG02 appears on days 6, 10, 14, 18)","source_spans":[{"path":"data/input.csv","start_line":6,"end_line":9,"quoted_text":"DG02,thermal,6,301.3,7.55,690\nDG02,thermal,10,316.3,7.49,742\nDG02,thermal,14,292.6,7.58,651\nDG02,thermal,18,311.4,7.61,604"},{"path":"data-description.md","start_line":20,"end_line":23,"quoted_text":"The four rows that share a digester_id are repeated measurements of the same\nphysical reactor and are not independent of one another; they differ only in the\nday the sample was drawn. Independent replication in this experiment is the\nvessel, of which there are twelve, six per pretreatment arm."}]}],"falsification_attempt":"I attempted to falsify the no-issue verdict by checking whether the reported statistics could actually stem from a hidden row-level (n = 48) analysis despite the vessel-level prose. Recomputation shows they cannot: (1) all 12 reported digester means reproduce exactly from the raw CSV session rows; (2) the six thermal vessel means (283.3-318.4) completely separate from the six control vessel means (239.5-271.4), for which the exact two-sided Mann-Whitney p is 2/C(12,6) = 2/924 = 0.0021645, matching the reported 0.002165, and U = 36.0 is exactly the 6x6 maximum; a 24-vs-24 row-level test would have a maximum U of 576 and, given the same complete separation in the raw rows, a far smaller p-value. (3) Code inspection confirms mannwhitneyu receives only the arm_values arrays built from the one-row-per-digester table, and no code path passes session-level rows to any inferential procedure. I also checked read_sessions for grouping errors (e.g., unit keys not stripped, or arm reassignment across rows) and found none; each digester_id maps to one arm and one mean.","cross_case_evidence_used":false,"unresolved_material_questions":[],"self_reported_confidence":"high"}]}